9,2075,15087,387,264,47311,1741,429,198,78045,70,955,2075,593,284,856,61,19,481,220,16,19,87,61,18,488,220,21,17,87,61,17,481,220,24,16,87,488,220,19,17,7110,60,9885,279,2629,315,678,3204,2750,315,400,69,7,16,15,47822,16,15,15,16630,3,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $g(x) = x^2 - 11x + 30,$ and let $f(x)$ be a polynomial such that\n\\[g(f(x)) = x^4 - 14x^3 + 62x^2 - 91x + 42.\\]Find the sum of all possible values of $f(10^{100}).$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"0972c0e98995acc74c63d8c3ca9dfa01a61cb8dd18ca31657f6114d89c5c423f"},"seconds":76.37793064117432,"seed":1058023257169030723,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we need to find the polynomial \\( f(x) \\) such that \\( g(f(x)) = x^4 - 14x^3 + 62x^2 - 91x + 42 \\) given \\( g(x) = x^2 - 11x + 30 \\).\n\nFirst, let's express \\( g(f(x)) \\) in terms of \\( f(x) \\):\n\\[\ng(f(x)) = (f(x))^2 - 11f(x) + 30.\n\\]\nWe are given that:\n\\[\ng(f(x)) = x^4 - 14x^3 + 62x^2 - 91x + 42.\n\\]\nThis implies:\n\\[\n(f(x))^2 - 11f(x) + 30 = x^4 - 14x^3 + 62x^2 - 91x + 42.\n\\]\n\nTo find \\( f(x) \\), we need a polynomial \\( f(x) \\) such that the above equation holds. Let's assume \\( f(x) \\) is a quadratic polynomial:\n\\[\nf(x) = ax^2 + bx + c.\n\\]\n\nThen,\n\\[\n(f(x))^2 = (ax^2 + bx + c)^2 = a^2x^4 + 2abx^3 + (2ac + b^2)x^2 + 2bcx + c^2.\n\\]\n\nNext, we compute \\( 11f(x) \\):\n\\[\n11f(x) = 11(ax^2 + bx + c) = 11ax^2 + 11bx + 11c.\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\\[\n(f(x))^2 - 11f(x) + 30 = a^2x^4 + 2abx^3 + (2ac + b^2 - 11a)x^2 + (2bc - 11b)x + (c^2 - 11c + 30).\n\\]\n\nWe equate this to the given polynomial:\n\\[\na^2x^4 + 2abx^3 + (2ac + b^2 - 11a)x^2 + (2bc - 11b)x + (c^2 - 11c + 30) = x^4 - 14x^3 + 62x^2 - 91x + 42.\n\\]\n\nBy comparing coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n1. \\( a^2 = 1 \\)\n2. \\( 2ab = -14 \\)\n3. \\( 2ac + b^2 - 11a = 62 \\)\n4. \\( 2bc - 11b = -91 \\)\n5. \\( c^2 - 11c + 30 = 42 \\)\n\nFrom the first equation:\n\\[\na^2 = 1 \\implies a = \\pm 1.\n\\]\n\n### Case 1: \\( a = 1 \\)\nFrom the second equation:\n\\[\n2b = -14 \\implies b = -7.\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\( a = 1 \\) and \\( b = -7 \\) into the third equation:\n\\[\n2c - 49 - 11 = 62 \\implies 2c - 60 = 62 \\implies 2c = 122 \\implies c = 61.\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\( b = -7 \\) into the fourth equation:\n\\[\n2(-7)c - 11(-7) = -91 \\implies -14c + 77 = -91 \\implies -14c = -168 \\implies c = 12.\n\\]\n\nThis contradicts \\( c = 61 \\). Thus, there is no solution for \\( a = 1 \\).\n\n### Case 2: \\( a = -1 \\)\nFrom the second equation:\n\\[\n-2b = -14 \\implies b = 7.\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\( a = -1 \\) and \\( b = 7 \\) into the third equation:\n\\[\n-2c + 49 + 11 = 62 \\implies -2c + 60 = 62 \\implies -2c = 2 \\implies c = -1.\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\( b = 7 \\) into the fourth equation:\n\\[\n2(7)c - 11(7) = -91 \\implies 14c - 77 = -91 \\implies 14c = -14 \\implies c = -1.\n\\]\n\nThis is consistent. Thus, \\( f(x) = -x^2 + 7x - 1 \\).\n\nFinally, we find \\( f(10^{100}) \\):\n\\[\nf(10^{100}) = -(10^{100})^2 + 7(10^{100}) - 1 = -10^{200} + 7 \\cdot 10^{100} - 1.\n\\]\n\nThe sum of all possible values of \\( f(10^{100}) \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-10^{200} + 7 \\cdot 10^{100} - 1}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{-10^{200} + 7 \\cdot 10^{100} - 1}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
